# Nautilus Kubernetes Redis Deployment

## 1. Project Overview

This project deploys Redis as an in-memory caching service inside a Kubernetes cluster for the Nautilus application development team.

The deployment uses the official `redis:alpine` image and Kubernetes ConfigMap configuration to set Redis maximum memory to 2 MB.

The deployment is intended for initial testing before a potential production rollout.

## 2. Objectives

- Create a ConfigMap named `my-redis-config`.
- Configure Redis with `maxmemory 2mb`.
- Deploy Redis using Kubernetes Deployment.
- Run exactly one replica.
- Configure the container name as `redis-container`.
- Request 1 CPU.
- Mount an `emptyDir` data volume.
- Mount the Redis ConfigMap.
- Expose container port 6379.
- Verify Redis is running and using the requested memory configuration.

